<title>FRANCE: French consumer prices unchanged in April.</title>
<headline>French consumer prices unchanged in April.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE</p>
<p>gave the following final data:</p>
<p>				    Apr	  Mar	 Apr 1996</p>
<p> Month-on-month inflation   0.0	  0.1	  0.2</p>
<p> Year-on-year inflation     0.9	  1.1	  2.4</p>
<p> CPI Index (base 1990)    115.0	115.0	114.0</p>
<p>				    Apr   Last 3 months  yr/yr</p>
<p> EU harmonised		  0.0	  0.4	  1.0</p>
<p> EU harmonised infl index   Apr	  Mar     Apr 96</p>
<p>				  101.1	101.1	100.1</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following breakdown of the consumer price index for all households in mainland France, base 1990 (not EU harmonised).</p>
<p>     Category		  Weight(pct) index  1-mo   3-mo  yr/yr</p>
<p> Food excluding tobacco	 20.20    108.0   0.2   -1.0    0.5</p>
<p> Private-sector manufactures  32.77    108.9  -0.1    1.4    0.0</p>
<p> Private-sector services	19.64    126.3   0.2    0.5    1.7</p>
<p> Energy				8.66    113.9  -0.9   -1.6    2.1</p>
<p> Public services ex energy     6.46    131.0   0.3    1.2    2.9</p>
<p> Rent, water			 6.68    130.4   0.0    0.4    1.6</p>
<p> Health spending		   5.59    110.2   0.2    0.1    0.5</p>
<p> Total excluding tobacco	98.02    114.0   0.0    0.4    0.8</p>
<p>NOTE: European Union harmonised data complies with definitions in the Maastricht treaty and is meant to allow comparisons between member states. Harmonised data was issued for the first time in March, with data for the month of January.</p>
<p>INSEE said on May 13 that consumer prices were unchanged to 0.1 percent higher in April, with a year-on-year rise of 0.9 percent to 1.0 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
